
================================================================================
                          THE SCRIPTORIUM
================================================================================

You step into a vast hall of scribes.  Rows of slanted
desks stretch into the distance, each piled with parchment.
This is where the dungeon's spells are COPIED and ORGANISED
-- the art of duplication and transmutation.

On the desk before you lies a single file:

    manuscript

================================================================================
                 THE SPELL OF DUPLICATION: cp
================================================================================

The 'cp' (copy) spell makes a duplicate of a file.  The
original stays where it is; a copy appears under a new name.

    cp SOURCE DEST

For example, to copy the manuscript into a backup:

    cp manuscript backup

Now run 'ls' and you will see BOTH 'manuscript' and 'backup'.
Scribes copy a scroll before editing it, so the original is
never lost.

================================================================================
                THE SPELL OF TRANSMUTATION: mv
================================================================================

The 'mv' (move) spell does two things.  It can RENAME a file:

    mv backup archive          # 'backup' becomes 'archive'

...or MOVE a file into another room (directory):

    mv archive somewhere/      # send 'archive' into 'somewhere'

Unlike 'cp', 'mv' does not leave the original behind -- the
file is transmuted from one name (or place) to another.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 cp  vs  mv
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    cp   duplicates  -> you end up with TWO files
    mv   relocates   -> you end up with ONE file, moved or renamed

================================================================================
                            PRACTICE
================================================================================

    1.  cp manuscript backup      Duplicate the manuscript
    2.  ls                        See both files
    3.  mv backup archive         Rename your copy
    4.  ls                        See the rename took effect

Master the scribes' craft, and no spell will ever be lost
to you again.

